<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4791" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bacchātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A celebrating of the orgies of Bacchus</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8</span></i>.—Hence. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A revelling</i>, <i>raving</i>, <i>in the manner of the Bacchœ</i> (rare):
			sileatur de nocturnis ejus baccationibus ac vigiliis, *
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 12, § 33</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
